+From 1975afee4af99085932dbb5c75ee6c798d8218e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:43:49 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 2/5] drm/panel: Add Samsung AMS678UW01 panel driver
+
+Add a driver for the Samsung AMS678UW01 DSC command mode panel used in
+the OnePlus 8 Pro (instantnoodlep). It was generated with
+linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator from the vendor device tree.
+
+The panel supports four vendor timings: 1080x2376 and 1440x3168 (panel
+internal scaling), each at 60 and 120 Hz. As the DSC configuration
+differs between them, the mode is selected at probe time with the
+"mode" module parameter (default: 1440x3168@120).
+
+Tested modes: 1080x2376@60, 1080x2376@120 and 1440x3168@120
+(kmscube: ~119.4 fps).
+
+Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |  12 +
+ drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile                |   1 +
+ .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams678uw01.c  | 464 ++++++++++++++++++
+ 3 files changed, 477 insertions(+)
+ create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams678uw01.c
+
